      "message": "🟡\nRead-only test silently skips on blank systems Medium\nThe test reads the current interface state and skips via Skip If if no Static/DHCP address is present. It never configures an address itself. On a freshly provisioned or CI-only BMC with no pre-existing address, the test always skips — providing zero coverage with no visible failure. A self-contained [Setup] / [Teardown] that configures and removes a static address would make the test unconditionally executable.\n🟢\nEmpty IPv4Addresses edge case not explicitly documented Low\nIf the interface returns zero IPv4Addresses entries, the skip guard correctly handles it (no Static/DHCP → skip). However, the [Documentation] does not mention this, which may confuse future readers who wonder whether the Should Not Contain assertion is safe on an empty list.\n🟢\n[Documentation] does not mention read-only / precondition nature Low\nThe docstring says \"Verify IPv4 link-local is not present when Static or DHCP IPv4 is configured\" but does not clarify that the test requires the system to already have such a configuration. Adding a note like \"Requires an existing Static or DHCP IPv4 address on the interface; otherwise the test is skipped.\" would aid triage of unexpected SKIP results in CI.",
